WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.279 --> 00:00:12.469
Imagine a country with the population of MANHATTAN but with huge reserves of oil and gas.

00:00:12.469 --> 00:00:16.480
A country surrounded by the wealthiest oil
rich monarchies.

00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:18.860
Where am I talking about?

00:00:18.860 --> 00:00:19.860
Exactly!

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:20.860
Bahrain!

00:00:20.860 --> 00:00:23.520
A country so tiny that we almost can’t see
it on the map.

00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:30.880
Yes, yes, I know what you’re thinking…
life must be wonderful here, right?

00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:36.570
Money for everybody, a prosperous economy
and amazing growth, right?

00:00:36.570 --> 00:00:44.500
Well… the opposite is true.

00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:49.260
Bahrain Downgraded To Junk, As Political Crackdown
Continues Unabated

00:00:49.260 --> 00:00:51.739
Yes, you heard that right.

00:00:51.739 --> 00:00:56.350
Bahrain debt is considered to be a junk bond
on the international market.

00:00:56.350 --> 00:01:01.010
This means, investors are so hesitant about
their economy that they don’t believe Bahrein

00:01:01.010 --> 00:01:03.649
will be able to give those loans back.

00:01:03.649 --> 00:01:07.000
The truth is… things in Bahrain are getting
really sour.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:10.740
If you’ve follow VisualPolitik for a long
time, you already know that, within the Islamic

00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:15.390
world, there are two big groups: SUNNI muslims
and SHIA muslims.

00:01:15.390 --> 00:01:18.130
And they hate each other.

00:01:18.130 --> 00:01:21.700
As you know, Saudi Arabia is something like
the SunnI Muslim Hollywood.

00:01:21.700 --> 00:01:26.590
And the Islamic Republic of Iran is the same
but for the Shia Muslims.

00:01:26.590 --> 00:01:35.040
This is why they have been in a cold war for
decades.

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:39.780
In the context of this cold war, Bahrain has
the funniest situation of all.

00:01:39.780 --> 00:01:42.939
Basically, in this country, the majority of
the population is SHIA muslim.

00:01:42.939 --> 00:01:46.570
But the Royal house that rules the country
is SUNNI muslim.

00:01:46.570 --> 00:01:52.009
This is why their monarchs have turned political
oppression into an art.

00:01:52.009 --> 00:01:53.009
OK!

00:01:53.009 --> 00:01:56.689
So far, nothing that will surprise you.

00:01:56.689 --> 00:01:57.689
But hey!

00:01:57.689 --> 00:01:58.760
The title of this video is…

00:01:58.760 --> 00:02:06.729
Why Bahrein could become the world’s wealthiest
country… or something like that.

00:02:06.729 --> 00:02:09.910
So why do we say that?

00:02:09.910 --> 00:02:13.980
Because of this.

00:02:13.980 --> 00:02:17.850
Bahrain discovers largest oil field in country
since 1932

00:02:17.850 --> 00:02:19.940
Yes, my dear viewers.

00:02:19.940 --> 00:02:21.800
They already already had dinosaur juice.

00:02:21.800 --> 00:02:24.230
But now they have even more.

00:02:24.230 --> 00:02:28.290
Basically, Bahrein could have more oil than
Russia itself.

00:02:28.290 --> 00:02:30.810
And with just a fraction of their population.

00:02:30.810 --> 00:02:35.070
So… in summary, there are only a few people
to share the money with.

00:02:35.070 --> 00:02:39.940
But the question is… is this ENOUGH to become
the wealthiest country on the planet?

00:02:39.940 --> 00:02:45.629
Why, even with so much oil, are Bahrain’s
debt bonds still considered junk?

00:02:45.629 --> 00:02:47.910
What is going on this country?

00:02:47.910 --> 00:02:52.780
Today we are going to answer to all of these
questions but before we do, let’s take a

00:02:52.780 --> 00:02:53.780
look back at history.

00:02:53.780 --> 00:02:59.780
A 
GOLDEN CAGE

00:02:59.780 --> 00:03:05.640
Look, if any of you want to become a dictador
one day, here are some tips.

00:03:05.640 --> 00:03:08.660
Basically, there are two ways to make people
follow you.

00:03:08.660 --> 00:03:11.420
The first one is the obvious one: good old
oppression.

00:03:11.420 --> 00:03:12.420
The problem?

00:03:12.420 --> 00:03:22.459
If you go too crazy with the oppression…
you’re risking a popular uprising.

00:03:22.459 --> 00:03:27.599
We told you thousands of times here on VisualPolitik,
being a dictator is a risky job.

00:03:27.599 --> 00:03:31.400
Not many of them die of old age.

00:03:31.400 --> 00:03:38.610
But… there is an alternative, healthier
and more sustainable way: what we can call

00:03:38.610 --> 00:03:40.939
the ‘money for nothing’ strategy.

00:03:40.939 --> 00:03:44.280
Basically, you shower all your citizens in
gold.

00:03:44.280 --> 00:03:48.040
If they’re wealthy and they don’t need
to get a job, they won’t worry about politics

00:03:48.040 --> 00:03:51.450
at all.

00:03:51.450 --> 00:03:57.610
So the AL KHALIFA family, the ruling family
in Bahrain, has combined both of these methods

00:03:57.610 --> 00:03:58.900
in a very effective fashion.

00:03:58.900 --> 00:04:03.209
In fact, the Prime Minister, who happens to
be the King’s uncle, holds the World record

00:04:03.209 --> 00:04:04.920
for the longest-lasting ruler.

00:04:04.920 --> 00:04:08.890
He has been in power since 1971.

00:04:08.890 --> 00:04:15.439
Nonetheless… how can a SUNNY muslim family
stay in power for such a long time in a country

00:04:15.439 --> 00:04:17.670
with a SHIA majority population?

00:04:17.670 --> 00:04:24.400
Well, as we said before, on one hand we have
that good old iron fist.

00:04:24.400 --> 00:04:26.470
Do you protest against the government?

00:04:26.470 --> 00:04:27.470
Good!

00:04:27.470 --> 00:04:31.990
You’ll automatically be considered a terrorist:
they’ll send you to jail, give you the death

00:04:31.990 --> 00:04:33.510
penalty, or just exile you.

00:04:33.510 --> 00:04:36.050
And we aren’t talking about an isolated
example here.

00:04:36.050 --> 00:04:43.919
This is something that happens every week.

00:04:43.919 --> 00:04:49.210
Bahrain strips 115 of nationality over 'terrorism'
allegations

00:04:49.210 --> 00:04:59.620
Over 700 people in Bahrain have had their
citizenship revoked since 2012

00:04:59.620 --> 00:05:04.630
And yes, I know what you’re going to say:
‘Oh, come on Simon, don’t be such a snowflake!

00:05:04.630 --> 00:05:08.300
In other democratic countries they’d retire
your citizenship too!’

00:05:08.300 --> 00:05:10.520
And, of course, you’re right.

00:05:10.520 --> 00:05:13.220
But the difference is the proportions.

00:05:13.220 --> 00:05:16.700
For example, in United Kingdom, there are
some examples, sure.

00:05:16.700 --> 00:05:19.860
But there are one, two… ten… here we’re
talking about hundreds.

00:05:19.860 --> 00:05:23.010
And OK, you might say now… ‘well, but
things are changing, right?

00:05:23.010 --> 00:05:27.289
The World is evolving, the Middle East is
getting more and more modern…’ well…

00:05:27.289 --> 00:05:31.210
sorry to say it but, in this case, the opposite
is true.

00:05:31.210 --> 00:05:37.390
In 2011, during the arab spring, the SHIA
citizens went to the streets asking for more

00:05:37.390 --> 00:05:40.190
democracy.

00:05:40.190 --> 00:05:45.520
Saudi Arabia, alongside with United Arab Emirates,
send troops to help the Bahraini government

00:05:45.520 --> 00:05:47.100
repress those demonstrations.

00:05:47.100 --> 00:05:52.789
So today, 1 out of every 500 people in Bahrain
are political prisoners.

00:05:52.789 --> 00:05:54.330
Among them there are many shia leaders.

00:05:54.330 --> 00:05:55.560
But not only that!

00:05:55.560 --> 00:06:00.770
Since 2011, Bahrein has passed new laws to
make it easier to retire one’s citizenship.

00:06:00.770 --> 00:06:06.500
And believe me, losing Bahreini citizenship
is a BIG shame.

00:06:06.500 --> 00:06:13.960
Losing citizenship means that you lose all
your Rights.

00:06:13.960 --> 00:06:19.410
You must give up your passport, your driving
license, you cannot own a house, a car, a

00:06:19.410 --> 00:06:21.210
phone or a bank account.

00:06:21.210 --> 00:06:22.960
You cannot marry in the country or have a
bank account.

00:06:22.960 --> 00:06:25.220
If you decide to leave, you cannot come back.

00:06:25.220 --> 00:06:28.229
And if you happen to stay, you cannot leave.

00:06:28.229 --> 00:06:31.819
In summary, opposing the government turns
you into a second class citizen.

00:06:31.819 --> 00:06:35.229
And… well… this is a big shame because,
my dear viewers, being a first class citizen

00:06:35.229 --> 00:06:37.630
is just GREAT.

00:06:37.630 --> 00:06:41.229
And this is where the ‘money for nothing’
policy comes into play.

00:06:41.229 --> 00:06:43.919
This is what we can call Bahrain’s social
contract.

00:06:43.919 --> 00:06:47.660
Basically, if you forget about politics, you
don’t have to worry about anything.

00:06:47.660 --> 00:06:49.130
Are you looking for a job?

00:06:49.130 --> 00:06:50.780
You can get it in the government!

00:06:50.780 --> 00:06:54.690
And don’t worry, nobody is going to check
if you even go to the office.

00:06:54.690 --> 00:07:00.639
Do you need to go to the supermarket?

00:07:00.639 --> 00:07:03.550
Everything is subsidized!

00:07:03.550 --> 00:07:06.150
Fuel your car?

00:07:06.150 --> 00:07:07.360
Crazy cheap prices!

00:07:07.360 --> 00:07:09.130
OK, OK!

00:07:09.130 --> 00:07:13.770
And what happens if you wanna work for a private
Business?

00:07:13.770 --> 00:07:14.770
No problem!

00:07:14.770 --> 00:07:16.889
The government guarantees quotes for local
workers.

00:07:16.889 --> 00:07:19.470
So no immigrant will take away your job!

00:07:19.470 --> 00:07:22.500
This is, actually, the funniest part: the
immigrant quotas.

00:07:22.500 --> 00:07:27.510
Basically, they are meant to reserve the coolest
Jobs for the locals.

00:07:27.510 --> 00:07:35.290
For example, 50% of Bank workers have to be
from Bahrain.

00:07:35.290 --> 00:07:37.500
In the cool, fancy shops, 30%.

00:07:37.500 --> 00:07:39.289
But construction workers?

00:07:39.289 --> 00:07:40.289
Just 5%!

00:07:40.289 --> 00:07:41.289
Why?

00:07:41.289 --> 00:07:43.790
Well… because who wants to lay bricks under
the Bahraini Sun?

00:07:43.790 --> 00:07:44.790
Oh!

00:07:44.790 --> 00:07:45.790
Let’s just leave that for the immigrants!

00:07:45.790 --> 00:07:48.490
This is why 55% of the Bahraini population
are immigrants.

00:07:48.490 --> 00:07:51.270
And they are the ones who actually get work
done.

00:07:51.270 --> 00:07:54.300
And… well… to be fair, I have to make
an aside here.

00:07:54.300 --> 00:07:57.849
Look, having more immigrants than locals is
very common in the Middle East.

00:07:57.849 --> 00:08:01.400
For example, foreign citizens make up 75%
of Qatar’s population.

00:08:01.400 --> 00:08:03.910
But Bahrain is a pioneer in one way.

00:08:03.910 --> 00:08:08.080
They are one of the few countries that ban
the so-called KAFALA.

00:08:08.080 --> 00:08:10.169
And what is KAFALA all about?

00:08:10.169 --> 00:08:13.680
Well… this is a sort of modern-day slavery.

00:08:13.680 --> 00:08:17.810
The KAFALA system links foreign workers with
a national who is their patron.

00:08:17.810 --> 00:08:22.380
This patron can decide whether the immigrant
can change his or her job or even leave the

00:08:22.380 --> 00:08:23.380
country.

00:08:23.380 --> 00:08:24.380
So well…

00:08:24.380 --> 00:08:28.250
Bahrain has abolished this inhuman practice
so… there you go.

00:08:28.250 --> 00:08:30.730
Nonetheless, despite all of this, what you
now might wonder is…

00:08:30.730 --> 00:08:34.539
Can a country where nobody Works prosper?

00:08:34.539 --> 00:08:44.240
And the answer is… of course not.

00:08:44.240 --> 00:08:51.100
120 DOLLARS
Living without working is expensive.

00:08:51.100 --> 00:08:55.980
They only manage it in Bahrain because of
one thing: OIL.

00:08:55.980 --> 00:09:03.380
Dinosaur juice makes up more than 60% of their
exports and 75% of the government’s income.

00:09:03.380 --> 00:09:07.710
But, in order to cover all the costs, the
Government needs the oil barrel price at 120

00:09:07.710 --> 00:09:08.710
dollars.

00:09:08.710 --> 00:09:11.670
Less than that and they don’t make enough
profit to make ends meet.

00:09:11.670 --> 00:09:13.560
And you might wonder…

00:09:13.560 --> 00:09:16.190
Is 120 dollars too much or too little?

00:09:16.190 --> 00:09:25.990
Well, look, at a historic peak, in July 2008,
oil was at 147 dollars.

00:09:25.990 --> 00:09:29.250
But, as you know, in 2014, oil prices fell.

00:09:29.250 --> 00:09:34.350
In January 2016, they went as little as 26
dollars.

00:09:34.350 --> 00:09:38.640
And this explains news like this.

00:09:38.640 --> 00:09:45.360
S&amp;P cuts Bahrain rating to ‘B+’
So what did they do with low prices and lack

00:09:45.360 --> 00:09:46.360
of income?

00:09:46.360 --> 00:09:48.840
Of course, they took on more and more debt.

00:09:48.840 --> 00:09:51.460
The result speaks for itself.

00:09:51.460 --> 00:09:55.190
In just two years, public debt has gone from
7% to 70%.

00:09:55.190 --> 00:09:58.940
And despite crude prices going up again…
it seems pretty unlikely that it will reach

00:09:58.940 --> 00:10:01.950
120 dollars a barrel anytime soon.

00:10:01.950 --> 00:10:12.650
So far, Bahrain has already revoked subsidies
on meat products… and this is just the beginning.

00:10:12.650 --> 00:10:17.650
Bahrain will introduce VAT by end of 2018,
says finance minister

00:10:17.650 --> 00:10:19.330
Yes, you heard that right.

00:10:19.330 --> 00:10:23.790
In Bahrain there is no tax on income and…
so far they didn’t even have indirect taxation.

00:10:23.790 --> 00:10:29.230
But the situation is desperate and they need
to create new taxes that didn’t even exist

00:10:29.230 --> 00:10:30.230
before.

00:10:30.230 --> 00:10:31.960
But… what can this mean for Bahrain?

00:10:31.960 --> 00:10:35.010
Well… do you remember how this particular
authoritarian rule worked?

00:10:35.010 --> 00:10:39.230
The Shia population accepts SUNNI oppression
in exchange for money for nothing.

00:10:39.230 --> 00:10:43.210
So when the economics fail… politics fail
too.

00:10:43.210 --> 00:10:51.790
Only a miracle could save the AL KHALIFA family…
and the miracle… is this one.

00:10:51.790 --> 00:10:58.500
THE OIL MIRACLE
So far, Bahrain produces 200 000 oil barrels

00:10:58.500 --> 00:10:59.500
a day.

00:10:59.500 --> 00:11:02.450
This is nothing compared with the 10’s of
millions in Saudi Arabia.

00:11:02.450 --> 00:11:06.140
But this is insane if we take the country’s
size into account.

00:11:06.140 --> 00:11:10.680
As I said before, Bahrain has just discovered
a big ass oil bed.

00:11:10.680 --> 00:11:15.520
And they could start pumping dinosaur juice
in less than five years.

00:11:15.520 --> 00:11:21.460
According to the most optimistic analysts,
this Could double production and end the deficit

00:11:21.460 --> 00:11:24.710
problem.

00:11:24.710 --> 00:11:25.710
The problem?

00:11:25.710 --> 00:11:29.990
If you follow VisualPolitik, you might have
already guessed it.

00:11:29.990 --> 00:11:37.190
Not every kind of oil costs the same.

00:11:37.190 --> 00:11:42.300
And this new oil bed has all the ingredients
needed to be very, very expensive.

00:11:42.300 --> 00:11:46.190
First of all, it’s underwater, which means
that Bahrain must build platforms on the seafloor.

00:11:46.190 --> 00:11:49.560
Second, it’s shale oil, which means it’s
under a rock.

00:11:49.560 --> 00:11:52.130
You need fracking technology to break that
rock.

00:11:52.130 --> 00:11:57.470
And that fracking technology is anything but
cheap.

00:11:57.470 --> 00:12:03.770
In this chart you can see the production cost
of an oil barrel in different countries.

00:12:03.770 --> 00:12:07.030
We can’t imagine how much fracking in Bahrain
would cost.

00:12:07.030 --> 00:12:11.280
But we can see how much it costs in United
States.

00:12:11.280 --> 00:12:17.210
If you pay attention to the chart, you’ll
see that shale oil is significantly more expensive

00:12:17.210 --> 00:12:20.340
than normal oil.

00:12:20.340 --> 00:12:24.070
If Bahrain wants to make a profit, the barrel
should cost over 60 dollars.

00:12:24.070 --> 00:12:28.870
But, since they need a huge profit to cover
all their expenses, they need an even higher

00:12:28.870 --> 00:12:30.090
market price.

00:12:30.090 --> 00:12:33.160
So what can save Bahrain from ruin?

00:12:33.160 --> 00:12:38.620
Well… the answer is the same as it is in
other Middle Eastern countries: diversification.

00:12:38.620 --> 00:12:40.200
Producing other things apart from oil.

00:12:40.200 --> 00:12:47.120
Which explains news like this.

00:12:47.120 --> 00:12:51.680
Mondelez opens $90m ‘Factory of the Future’
in Bahrain

00:12:51.680 --> 00:12:56.920
But, of course, if you really want to attract
Business from other industries, you need something

00:12:56.920 --> 00:12:58.010
other than oil beds.

00:12:58.010 --> 00:13:01.870
You need rule of law, with clear taxes and
a government that doesn’t send people to

00:13:01.870 --> 00:13:03.240
jail without a trial.

00:13:03.240 --> 00:13:08.390
We’ve told you this several times: Dubai
and, generally speaking, the United Arab Emirates,

00:13:08.390 --> 00:13:10.050
started this path years ago.

00:13:10.050 --> 00:13:12.460
Not Saudi Arabia might follow suit…

00:13:12.460 --> 00:13:14.690
although… we aren’t sure about that.

00:13:14.690 --> 00:13:18.510
And it’s a matter of time that Bahrain did
the same.

00:13:18.510 --> 00:13:22.890
But of course, if those economic reforms mean
that Bahraini people have to pay taxes or

00:13:22.890 --> 00:13:30.000
even… work hard… then the ruling family
will be in dire straits.

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:34.380
So the big question here is…

00:13:34.380 --> 00:13:39.250
Do you think the Bahraini citizens will accept
such an authoritarian government if they no

00:13:39.250 --> 00:13:42.060
longer enjoy the money for nothing policy?

00:13:42.060 --> 00:13:44.420
Do you think they’ll find a way to reform
their system?

